---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="A new default for the web">
<section class="prose"><p><strong>RevaCSS / foundation alpha</strong></p><h1>A new default<br/>for the web.</h1><p>Write meaningful HTML. Start with a complete design. Make it your own through a few tokens.</p><div class="row"><a class="button" href={`${base}guide/`}>Get started</a><a href={`${base}plain/`}>Inspect plain HTML</a></div></section>
<hr/>
<div class="grid"><article class="card"><h2>Native foundations</h2><p>Real buttons, forms, tables and disclosures. No runtime JavaScript.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Adaptive design</h2><p>Device-aware light and dark appearances, intrinsic layouts and local overrides.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Minimal decisions</h2><p>One stylesheet. Useful defaults. Ordinary CSS overrides.</p></article></div>
<h2>Review the foundation</h2><p>Open the reference pages directly or inspect these isolated previews. Text inside previews uses the same stylesheet.</p>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Light</h3><iframe title="Light native HTML preview" src={`${base}preview/light/`} width="600" height="600" loading="lazy"></iframe></section><section><h3>Dark</h3><iframe title="Dark native HTML preview" src={`${base}preview/dark/`} width="600" height="600" loading="lazy"></iframe></section></div>
<h2>Components in development</h2><p><a href={`${base}components/top-menu/`}>Top menu</a> adds responsive navigation with nested dropdowns, using only native HTML and CSS.</p>
<h2>Optional materials</h2><p><a href={`${base}themes/glass/`}>Glass material</a> adds frosted surfaces to the existing themes and shared attributes. <a href={`${base}preview/glass/light/`}>Explore light glass</a> or <a href={`${base}preview/glass/dark/`}>dark glass</a>.</p>
<h2>Current milestone</h2><p>This is an implementation preview, not the final component library or an accessibility certification. Foundations, documented presets, cards, layouts, forms, tables and top navigation are ready for review. Glass is available as an optional extension. More components, icons and multilingual font packs follow later. npm publication stays on hold until the first fully functional release is complete and tested.</p>
</Layout>
